• Build strong relationships with Clients and Partners;
• Provide a high standard of service to clients and partners;
• Engage with and support First Time Traded (FTT) clients to ensure a positive onboarding and trading experience;
• Build relationships with clients and partners in line with the Company’s hospitality and compliance policies;
• Support business development through approved marketing and social media channels;
• Coordinate and work with internal and external stakeholders;
• Provide reports for management and key Partners;
• Adhere to all relevant regulatory and compliance rules; and
• The responsibilities listed above are not exhaustive and may evolve in line with business needs. The role holder may be required to undertake additional duties reasonably consistent with the nature and seniority of the role.
Requirements

Key Skills:
• 3+ years’ experience in the retail derivatives industry
• 5+ years of sales experience
• Proven experience of regular targets being met
• In depth understanding of spread betting and CFDs
• Committed to delivering the highest possible service to clients
• Positive, self-motivated, KPI driven, and able to manage personal workload
• Experience with CRM use, preferably HubSpot
Benefits
• Competitive salary, and discretionary annual bonus.
• Private healthcare.
• Active Lifestyle allowance.
• Annual leave above minimum entitlement.
• Up to 3 weeks allowance to work in any location.

